  "body": "Orabona v10 Chapter 1 states that logarithmic guessing regret is unavoidable, without printing a minimax proof there. This package constructs a policy-independent binary history law and proves its normalization, count moments and variance. The actual strict-past predictions and the shared empirical-mean comparator then give expected signed cumulative regret at least `H(T+1)/6`. For every probability seed law and every causal policy whose output is measurable in the seed at each history and lies pointwise in `[0,1]`, the proof produces one fixed length-`T` binary sequence outside the seed integral with **seed-expected regret** at least `log(T+2)/6`, for `T ≥ 1`. Both coefficients are derived support for the qualitative source claim, not printed or claimed sharp.\n\nThe module reuses the existing regret, empirical mean and finite-action probability APIs. It adds 48 public proofs and 10 definitions, with 16 named nondegenerate canaries. The public and Test roots and the source-qualified Book route use the shared Lean graph. All 10,835 old registry IDs, URLs and statement hashes are preserved; the new registry entries comprise 58 public nodes and one explicit private source identity. The original eight reader cards and four curated declaration IDs remain intact.\n\nValidation passed: focused public/canary builds; 76 named standard-only axiom audits; 64 closed proposition and 12 definition identities; 64 native statement guards; 30 specified compiler VALUE dependency pairs; combined root and Tests; full harness (472 tests, seven existing skips); scoped frontier/shadow; nonvacuous exact-base contributor gate; and the clean Lean-verified site/registry with 13 inspected current panels. The distinct required automated blind decoder completed reconstruction. The anti-anchored source reviewer accepted the CONTRACT, BODY and FINAL packets with explicit source delta, and discharged R1–R8 individually. The actors reuse staged history; these are not human, external or runtime-attested reviews. Native safe-verify scans headers/source and does not compile Lean. Failed attempts, including the publication audit ordering failure, and versioned repairs are retained.\n\nStacked on OPEN, unmerged PR #190, exact head `9425fecb38be60b1acb7a918cb149f72117133ad`, branch `codex/research-online-regret-domains`. This PR closes only `C1-LOG-UNAVOIDABLE`. Chapter 1 still has 16 source inventory items and an unknown mandatory proof total; full regret/minimum, NoRegret and six other main-relative contributor gaps remain required and unwaived. Chapter 2 is incomplete; Chapters 3–16 and necessary appendix dependencies remain outstanding. The whole-book Goal stays active. Merge, deployment and main/live updates have not occurred.\n\nReview entry points: `BanditRLProof/OnlineGuessingLogLower.lean`, `Tests/OnlineGuessingLogLowerCanary.lean`, `docs/contracts/online-guessing-log-lower-v1`, and `runs/online-log-lower-20261008/{accepted-decision-v1.json,accepted-binding-audit-v1.json,accepted-reader-discharge-v1.json,final-reader-review-v1.md}`. The Book mapping and proof dependency evidence are separate from the curated teaching graph. No Functor Hypergraph discovery is claimed; the affected route shows the exact lower-bound scope and remaining obligations.\n",
